From 4387e6526102c2046bef9fcc8d10dbf1f1b5d289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:55:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen4exp/hc-mix: fused BF16 hyper-connection mixer and
 combine up to 16 tokens

Several concurrent speculative streams verify 9-16 tokens per step (4 users x (1 + 3 drafts) = 16).
Above 8 tokens the mixer fell back to the unfused BF16 chain (generic mmvf, ~118 us per mixer vs
~41 us fused at 8).  The BF16 mixer and the combine now serve up to HC_BF16_MAX_TOKENS = 16; the
launcher runs a 9-16-token batch as chunks of at most 8 tokens through the existing kernels (every
token is computed independently, so a chunk is bit-identical to one launch; a single 16-token
instantiation was slower, ~94 us for the down/inject kernel).  The Q8_0 variant keeps 8.

Bit-identical: output and first-token probabilities for prompts of exactly 4, 8, 9..16, 17, 24
tokens match the previous build; greedy sha unchanged.  IQ3_XXS all-VRAM -sm tensor, 600-token
greedy chats, mean of 3: 3 users 163.9 -> 169.3, 4 users 160.8 -> 168.6, 6 users 146.9 -> 158.6;
1-2 users unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
